# Workflows that stay enabled on the temporarybeasts/phoenix fork.
#
# The fork inherits every workflow in Arize-ai/phoenix, and most of them need
# Arize-only infrastructure (Slack webhooks, GitHub App tokens, Anthropic /
# OpenAI keys, the `oss-4-core-runner` runner, a `main` branch this fork
# doesn't have). Rather than editing those upstream files -- which would
# conflict on every nightly rebase -- .github/workflows/rbac-fork-workflow-guard.yml
# disables (via the Actions API, i.e. repo state, not file content) every
# workflow whose path is NOT listed here. New upstream workflows are picked up
# automatically after the next nightly rebase.
#
# To re-enable a workflow: add its path here AND run
#   gh workflow enable <file> -R temporarybeasts/phoenix
# (the guard only disables; it never re-enables).
#
# One path per line; `#` starts a comment.

# Fork-owned
.github/workflows/rbac-fork-nightly-rebase.yml
.github/workflows/rbac-fork-workflow-guard.yml

# Upstream PR checks that run without Arize secrets
.github/workflows/python-CI.yml
.github/workflows/typescript-CI.yml
.github/workflows/zizmor.yml
.github/workflows/openapi-schema.yaml
.github/workflows/pull-requests.yaml
.github/workflows/phoenix-sqlean-ci.yml
.github/workflows/helm-ci.yml
